sp.","arc":"Begins as a confident dealmaker who assumes all people can be bought. When Isolde rejects his offer to cancel her wind-debt, his plan unravels and the Cartel's princes blame him. He ends exposed and desperate, forced to confront that his price-based worldview has left him with no allies.","personality_traits":["smooth","calculating","ambitious","insecure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Mastery","description":"Tracks debts, tolls and favours across the archipelago in his head.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Negotiates and persuades with polished charm.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_tamsin_orchard","name":"Tamsin Orchard","description":"A stout, sunburned elder miller of the Hollow Circle in her sixties, with flour-dusted braids and a booming laugh. She lived through the aftermath of the Great Calm as a child and carries its lessons of self-reliance.","role":"supporting","motivation":"To protect the Hollow's grain and the people who depend on it from Cartel exploitation.","goal":"Organise the Hollow Circle to resist the Grain Levy and secure independent bridge access.","flaw":"She distrusts outsiders so deeply that she refuses help that could save her people.","internal_conflict":"She preaches self-reliance but knows the Hollow cannot survive without trade across the skybridges.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy strips the Hollow's harvest, and wind-debts keep her millers bound to Cartel lanes.","arc":"Starts as a suspicious holdout who refuses outside alliances. When Marlowe's chart reaches the Hollow and shows a route that bypasses Cartel lanes, Tamsin must choose between pride and survival. She ends by allying the Hollow Circle with the Wardens and breaking the Levy's grip.","personality_traits":["sturdy","blunt","warm","suspicious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Reckoning","description":"Judges harvests and storage needs with uncanny accuracy.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Community Rally","description":"Draws the Hollow's farmers together around a common cause.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_decimus_pursues_isolde","source_character_id":"chr_decimus_rook","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Decimus Rook holds Isolde Vane's family wind-debt and tries to buy or coerce the cylinder from her, setting the Cartel factor against the courier."},{"id":"rel_isolde_trusts_marlowe","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_marlowe_quill","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Vane delivers the cylinder to Marlowe Quill and gradually trusts her to read it, forming an alliance built on shared risk."},{"id":"rel_corvin_mentors_marlowe","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_halewright","target_character_id":"chr_marlowe_quill","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Corvin Halewright, a senior Warden, guides Marlowe Quill by explaining the weave patterns, though his rigid tradition clashes with her new theories."},{"id":"rel_decimus_pressures_marlowe","source_character_id":"chr_decimus_rook","target_character_id":"chr_marlowe_quill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Decimus Rook threatens Silverspine's funding to force Marlowe Quill to stop work on the cylinder's chart."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_distrusts_decimus","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orchard","target_character_id":"chr_decimus_rook","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tamsin Orchard resists the Grain Levy that Decimus Rook enforces on the Hollow's harvests."},{"id":"rel_marlowe_aids_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_marlowe_quill","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orchard","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Marlowe Quill, born to a Hollow milling family, sends her drift chart to Tamsin Orchard so the Hollow Circle can bypass Cartel lanes."}]}
