[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_venn","name":"Mara Venn","description":"A forty-year-old salvage captain from Mistral Docks, weathered by years of hauling wreckage between drifting isles. She has a burn scar along her left forearm from a forge accident, cropped grey-streaked hair, and wears a patched Cartel-issue coat she never paid off. Her crew is her family, and her wind-debts are heavy.","role":"protagonist","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","motivation":"To clear her crushing wind-debt to the Drift Cartel so her crew is no longer indentured to it.","goal":"Recover the liner's vaulted cargo and sell it to settle the debt before the season ends.","flaw":"Stubborn greed disguised as responsibility; she refuses to abandon a payday even when warned.","internal_conflict":"She believes she is protecting her crew, yet her choices keep putting them in mortal danger.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's debt collectors expect payment, while the fog-bound liner hunts her crew from within.","arc":"Mara begins by pushing her crew deeper into the liner for the cargo that would erase her debt. When the liner traps Joss and offers to release him in exchange for the vault's contents, she chooses to abandon the cargo and cut the liner's moorings. She ends poorer and still indebted, but trusted by her crew and free of her obsession with the payday.","personality_traits":["stubborn","protective","pragmatic","haunted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fog Navigation","description":"Reads wind and drift patterns to guide a vessel through zero-visibility fog.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Crew Command","description":"Holds a frightened crew together under pressure.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_joss_tamber","name":"Joss Tamber","description":"A twenty-four-year-old rigger and Mara's youngest crew member, lanky and nervous, with ink-stained fingers from sketching bridge-cable knots. He trained briefly with the Bridge Wardens before being dismissed for a failed inspection.","role":"supporting","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","motivation":"To redeem his name and regain a place among the Bridge Wardens.","goal":"Find proof of the liner's original cloudstone rigging to present to the Wardens as a discovery.","flaw":"Reckless curiosity that overrides his caution.","internal_conflict":"He fears he is the incompetent engineer the Wardens judged him to be.","external_conflict":"The liner's presence lures him toward its oldest, most dangerous decks while the Wardens' reputation bars him from home.","arc":"Joss starts as an anxious rigger desperate to prove himself. When the liner's whispers speak to him in his dead mentor's voice and lead him to the rigging hold, he must choose between his hunger for vindication and Mara's order to retreat. He obeys, ending as a rigger who values living crewmates over recognition.","personality_traits":["anxious","curious","earnest","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Reading","description":"Judges the stress and integrity of cloudstone rigging by touch and sound.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_ondra_hale","name":"Ondra Hale","description":"A weary sixty-year-old former purser whose spirit, or something wearing it, still walks the liner. Pale and unnaturally still, she wears a faded uniform that never seems to dampen in the fog. She has been bound to the ship since the night it vanished.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","motivation":"To keep the liner crewed so it never drifts into the empty sky alone again.","goal":"Bind Mara's salvage crew to the ship as its new complement.","flaw":"Possessive loneliness that turns care into captivity.","internal_conflict":"She longs to be released from the ship but fears being forgotten if it ends.","external_conflict":"Salvagers' tools threaten to strip the liner, while Mara's crew keep resisting her hospitality.","arc":"Ondra begins as a gracious host who lulls intruders into staying. When Mara offers to cut the moorings and carry the ship's name back to Mistral Docks, Ondra faces the possibility of being remembered rather than kept. She finally lets the crew go, dissolving into the fog as her loneliness is answered.","personality_traits":["gracious","melancholic","unsettling","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fog Whisper","description":"Speaks in voices of the dead through the fog to draw victims deeper into the ship.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Ship Memory","description":"Knows every corridor and cabin of the liner and shifts them at will.","category":"supernatural"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_oakes","name":"Bram Oakes","description":"A broad, taciturn fifty-year-old Cartel enforcer who trails the crew to collect on Mara's debt. He has a thick grey beard, a coat lined with Cartel seals, and a past as a Hollow Circle miller's son before taking Cartel coin.","role":"supporting","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","motivation":"To secure Cartel favour so his family's grain debts to the Cartel are forgiven.","goal":"Seize the liner's cargo on the Cartel's behalf and bring Mara in.","flaw":"Blind obedience to whoever holds his debt.","internal_conflict":"He is ashamed of turning on the farming folk he came from.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy squeezes his family while the liner threatens his mission and his life.","arc":"Bram begins as a loyal collector who sees the crew as targets. When the fog traps him in a cabin where he hears his mother's voice recalling the grain levy, he must choose between taking the cargo and saving Joss. He drops the Cartel's orders to help the crew escape, ending as a man who acts on his own conscience.","personality_traits":["gruff","dutiful","guilt-ridden","stoic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Brawler","description":"Fights in close quarters with great strength and endurance.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_joss_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_joss_tamber","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Mara Venn took Joss Tamber on after the Wardens dismissed him and acts as his mentor, but her greed for the cargo makes her put him in harm's way."},{"id":"rel_ondra_mara_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_ondra_hale","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ondra Hale sees Mara Venn as the captain she must claim for the ship, and tempts her with the vault's cargo to keep her aboard."},{"id":"rel_bram_mara_rival","source_character_id":"chr_bram_oakes","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Bram Oakes is the Cartel's debt collector pursuing Mara Venn, and his orders to seize her cargo set him against her crew."},{"id":"rel_ondra_joss_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_ondra_hale","target_character_id":"chr_joss_tamber","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ondra Hale lures Joss Tamber with a dead mentor's voice, trying to make him the first of the crew to stay on the liner."}]}
</Output>
