{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vell","name":"Mara Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered skybridge pathfinder in her late thirties, born on the Hollow and trained at Mistral Docks. She has a sun-cracked face, a braided rope of dark hair, and a coat patched with cloudstone thread. Years ago she guided a survey party into an overgrown drifting isle and returned alone, and she has refused all expedition work since.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep anyone else from dying the way her last party did, and to pay off the wind-debt that binds her to the Cartel.","goal":"Guide the expedition to the jungle ruins and bring every member back alive, clearing her debt in the process.","flaw":"She hoards information and refuses to share what she knows, even when sharing would save lives.","internal_conflict":"She believes her silence once killed her party, yet she still cannot make herself speak openly about the jungle.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel has bought up her wind-debt and will forgive it only if she delivers the expedition to the ruins, whatever the cost to its members.","arc":"Mara starts as a guarded guide who keeps the jungle's dangers to herself. Midway through, the Cartel's agent orders her to abandon stragglers to meet the toll deadline, and she instead tells the whole party the full truth about her earlier failure. She ends as an open, trusted leader who accepts the debt's consequences rather than sacrifice others.","personality_traits":["wry","guarded","resourceful","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Jungle Pathfinding","description":"Reads overgrown terrain and shifting vines to find safe routes across a drifting isle.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Cloudstone Knotwork","description":"Ties emergency skybridge rigging that holds under heavy wind.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_dray","name":"Corvin Dray","role":"antagonist","description":"A sleek Cartel factor in his fifties with silver-ringed fingers and a tailored storm-coat. He rose from dock clerk to enforcer of the Cartel's most profitable lanes. He is certain the lost city holds cloudstone deposits that would cement the Cartel's power.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the city's cloudstone for the Cartel and win a seat among its merchant princes.","goal":"Seize the ruins' cloudstone before the Bridge Wardens or anyone else can claim it.","flaw":"Greed makes him ignore warnings and treat people as disposable ledger entries.","internal_conflict":"He fears that without the Cartel's favour he is still the powerless clerk he once was.","external_conflict":"The Toll War leaves the Cartel under pressure from the Bridge Wardens, and he needs this find to prove his worth before the Cartel council.","arc":"Corvin begins as a confident dealmaker who sees the jungle as a resource. When the ruins turn on his hired guards and he is stranded, he must choose between the cloudstone and his life, and he clings to the cargo. The jungle claims him, ending his arc as a cautionary figure whose greed destroys him.","personality_traits":["polished","calculating","impatient","ruthless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Binds people to him by buying and calling in their wind-debts.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_penn","name":"Isolde Penn","role":"supporting","description":"A young cartographer in her twenties from Silverspine Academy, with ink-stained hands and a satchel of charcoal and vellum. She is brilliant but has never left the academy's reading rooms. She is leading the scholarly side of the expedition.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To chart the lost city and prove that the skybridge network once reached beyond the known isles.","goal":"Map the ruins completely and carry the chart back to the Academy.","flaw":"Naive faith in books makes her dismiss field experience and ignore danger.","internal_conflict":"She wants to be a true explorer but is terrified of leaving the safety of theory.","external_conflict":"The Bridge Wardens want the map to bolster their side of the Toll War, and Corvin Dray wants it for the Cartel.","arc":"Isolde starts as a bookish theorist who trusts maps over people. When a chart leads the party into a vine-choked ravine and Mara's advice saves them, she admits the map was wrong. She finishes as a field-savvy cartographer who corrects her charts with firsthand observation.","personality_traits":["curious","earnest","anxious","bright"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts and predicts the drift of isles and bridge routes.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_ember","name":"Tobias Ember","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost with soot-darkened forearms and a limp from a snapped cable. He was assigned to inspect any bridge-structures found in the ruins and to watch the Cartel's movements.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To protect the skybridges from Cartel exploitation and honour the Wardens' oath.","goal":"Secure the ruins' old bridge-works so the Cartel cannot weaponise them in the Toll War.","flaw":"Rigid loyalty to the Wardens' rules makes him unable to adapt when circumstances demand it.","internal_conflict":"He starts to suspect the Wardens' orders are as self-serving as the Cartel's.","external_conflict":"His orders clash with the Cartel's contract, and he must keep an eye on Corvin while the jungle breaks his equipment.","arc":"Tobias begins as an unbending rule-follower. After a spark from his forge-kit threatens to sever an ancient span, he realises the rules protect nothing if followed blindly and breaks protocol to rescue the group. He ends as a pragmatic engineer who values lives over orders.","personality_traits":["stoic","loyal","blunt","dependable"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Braiding","description":"Repairs and braids cloudstone cable under pressure.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Spark Discipline","description":"Handles forge-kits safely and spots fire hazards before they ignite.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_corvin_debt","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_dray","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Dray holds Mara Vell's wind-debt and uses it to force her to guide the expedition against her judgment."},{"id":"rel_mara_isolde_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_penn","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Mara Vell reluctantly teaches Isolde Penn to read the jungle, and her lessons slowly replace Isolde's reliance on charts."},{"id":"rel_tobias_corvin_rival","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_ember","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_dray","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tobias Ember watches Corvin Dray as a Bridge Warden and Cartel factor on opposite sides of the Toll War."},{"id":"rel_tobias_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_ember","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tobias Ember grows from distrust to alliance with Mara Vell as her honesty earns his respect."}]}
