t in authority figures who flatter his competence.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between his oath of Warden neutrality and his growing conviction that he must take a side.","external_conflict":"Cartel enforcers and Vane's agents target Wardens who speak against the tolls.","arc":"He starts as an apolitical craftsman who passes Valeria information without understanding how she uses it. When he is arrested in the Toll War crackdown, he learns he was a pawn. He chooses to testify publicly about toll corruption despite the risk, ending as a confident advocate who trusts his own judgment.","personality_traits":["earnest","precise","shy","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and repairing cloudstone cables.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_odalys_marrin","name":"Odalys Marrin","description":"A matriarch in her sixties who leads the Hollow Circle from The Hollow. Her hands are calloused from decades at the windmills, and she speaks slowly and with great authority.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect the farmers who survived the Great Calm and keep the archipelago fed.","goal":"Defeat the Cartel's Grain Levy without sparking open violence.","flaw":"Stubborn isolationism and a distrust of anyone from outside the Hollow.","internal_conflict":"She must choose between her community's self-reliance and the alliances she needs to survive.","external_conflict":"The Cartel levy and Vane's enforcers threaten to seize the harvest.","arc":"She begins as a wary leader who refuses to deal with outsiders. When Vane's enforcers move on the grain stores, she must decide whether to trust Valeria's offer of an alliance. She agrees, shares the Circle's grain records with the Senate, and ends as a leader who accepts that self-reliance includes choosing allies.","personality_traits":["patient","stubborn","protective","wise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Harvest Networks","description":"Coordinates grain shipments and quiet supply routes across the isles.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_valeria_vane_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","target_character_id":"chr_brennick_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Valeria Corvane schemes to dismantle Brennick Vane's rise, and he treats her as the discredited elite he rallies crowds against."},{"id":"rel_vane_valeria_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_brennick_vane","target_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Brennick Vane sees Valeria Corvane as the chief obstacle to emergency powers and moves to ruin her through his followers."},{"id":"rel_valeria_tomas_ally","source_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","target_character_id":"chr_tomas_reeve","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Valeria Corvane uses Tomas Reeve as a source inside the Wardens, exploiting his trust while he believes she is a mentor."},{"id":"rel_valeria_odalys_ally","source_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","target_character_id":"chr_odalys_marrin","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Valeria Corvane seeks Odalys Marrin's grain records as evidence, and Odalys cautiously weighs the alliance."},{"id":"rel_odalys_vane_rival","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_marrin","target_character_id":"chr_brennick_vane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Odalys Marrin resists the Grain Levy that Brennick Vane enforces for the Cartel, putting her at odds with him."}]}
