{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_wren_halloway","name":"Wren Halloway","description":"A weathered, soft-spoken traveller in her late thirties, born on The Hollow to a family of millers. After a failed harvest left her family deep in wind-debt, she took up long solitary crossings to repay it. She is lean and sun-browned, wears a patched grey coat, and carries a satchel of salvaged glass shards that she never explains.","role":"protagonist","motivation":"To repay her family's crushing wind-debt before the season turns so her siblings are not bound into Cartel labour.","goal":"Complete the long crossing to Mistral Docks and deliver the glass cargo that will settle the debt.","flaw":"She refuses all help and trusts only her own endurance, even when it endangers her.","internal_conflict":"She fears that accepting kindness will make her a debtor in spirit as well as in law.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls and levies make every crossing costlier, and the season deadline keeps shrinking.","arc":"Wren begins as an isolated traveller who rations every word and refuses aid. At a collapsing skybridge crossing, where the Toll War has left maintenance neglected, she must accept a Warden's rope or fall, and she lets Tobias save her. She ends the journey willing to share the load of her debt with her community, and to accept help without shame.","personality_traits":["stoic","observant","stubborn","laconic","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windreading","description":"She reads wind currents and bridge tension by feel and sound, and can tell when a crossing is about to fail.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Long Endurance","description":"She can travel for days on little water and rest, a skill honed by her years of crossings.","category":"physical"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"},{"id":"chr_tobias_vane","name":"Tobias Vane","description":"A broad-shouldered Bridge Warden engineer in his fifties, raised in the forges of Emberroost. His hands are scarred from braiding cloudstone cable. He patrols the failing spans alone after his crew was reassigned, and speaks in short, practical sentences.","role":"supporting","motivation":"To keep the skybridges standing so no traveller is lost to the drop, as his brother once was.","goal":"Reinforce the most dangerous span before it collapses, with or without Warden funding.","flaw":"He cannot delegate or admit when a task is beyond him, and overworks himself.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between his oath to the Wardens and his anger at an order that abandons the bridges he loves.","external_conflict":"The Toll War starves the Wardens of resources while the Cartel profits from the bridges he maintains.","arc":"Tobias starts as a lone, exhausted loyalist who clings to the Wardens' failing orders. When Wren's crossing nearly kills her on his unrepaired span, he is forced to confront that his silence helps no one. He ends by speaking publicly against the Warden leadership and asking the Hollow Circle for aid to rebuild.","personality_traits":["gruff","dutiful","weary","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"He braids and repairs skybridge cables with expert speed.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Structural Sense","description":"He can judge a span's strength by its sway and hum.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_marguerite_quill","name":"Marguerite Quill","description":"A polished Drift Cartel collector in her forties from Mistral Docks, always dressed in dark silk with a ledger at her belt. She holds the Halloway debt and is known for patience that feels like a trap.","role":"antagonist","motivation":"To expand the Cartel's hold on every crossing and prove her worth to the merchant princes who passed her over.","goal":"Collect Wren's debt in labour so the Halloway family is bound to the Cartel's shipping lanes.","flaw":"She sees every person as an account to be balanced and cannot value anything unpriced.","internal_conflict":"She privately doubts that the Cartel's tolls are just, yet she silences that doubt to keep her standing.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy resistance by the Hollow Circle threatens her quota, and the Wardens challenge her tolls.","arc":"Marguerite begins as a confident debt collector who treats Wren as a ledger entry. When Wren arrives at the docks having crossed a ruined span, and the Hollow Circle refuses the levy together, Marguerite sees her system fail. She ends by quietly waiving part of the Halloway debt, an act that breaks her rigid accounting.","personality_traits":["calculating","poised","patient","ambitious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Mind","description":"She recalls every debt, rate, and due date without notes.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Persuasive Pressure","description":"She negotiates by making refusal feel costly.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_quill_holds_wren_debt","source_character_id":"chr_marguerite_quill","target_character_id":"chr_wren_halloway","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Marguerite Quill holds the Halloway wind-debt and pressures Wren Halloway to repay it in Cartel labour, driving Wren's desperate crossing."},{"id":"rel_tobias_rescues_wren","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_vane","target_character_id":"chr_wren_halloway","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tobias Vane rescues Wren Halloway on a failing span, forcing her to accept help and pulling him into her fight against the tolls."},{"id":"rel_tobias_opposes_quill","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_vane","target_character_id":"chr_marguerite_quill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tobias Vane resents Marguerite Quill's Cartel tolls, which drain the Wardens' resources and leave the bridges he maintains in disrepair."}]}
