ings stamped with the Cartel Charter seal. Raised on the Mistral Docks among shipping ledgers, he inherited his house's lanes and the debts that come with them.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep his family's shipping house solvent and respected among the Cartel princes.","goal":"Secure guaranteed trade lanes by joining the alliance while keeping tolls profitable.","flaw":"Greed leads him to treat every relationship as a transaction.","internal_conflict":"He suspects the tolls are bleeding the isles dry but fears his house will collapse without them.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy has turned the Hollow Circle against him, and rival Cartel princes pressure him to hold firm.","arc":"Corvin starts as a profiteer defending the levy. When the Hollow Circle halts grain shipments and his docks begin to starve, he chooses to waive the levy publicly in exchange for the alliance. He ends as a merchant who accepts lower profit for a stable realm.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","anxious","persuasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane Brokering","description":"Negotiates shipping and toll agreements that bend rivals to his terms.","category":"social"},{"name":"Ledger Mind","description":"Tracks complex debts and wind-debt balances without notes.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tessa_holloway","name":"Tessa Holloway","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered miller of the Hollow Circle in her fifties, Tessa has flour-dusted forearms, a braid of straw-coloured hair, and a calm voice. She survived the tales of the Great Calm as a child and carries its lessons of self-reliance.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep the archipelago fed and her community independent of Cartel control.","goal":"Have the Grain Levy abolished and win the Hollow a voice in the alliance.","flaw":"Deep distrust makes her refuse compromise even when offered fair terms.","internal_conflict":"She values quiet neutrality but knows the Hollow cannot survive the enemy alone.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy drains her mills, and the alliance demands she cooperate with those she resents.","arc":"Tessa begins by withholding grain as protest. After seeing Mistral Docks nearly starve, she chooses to release her stores to the alliance and accepts Corvin's waiver. She ends as an engaged leader who trades isolation for shared security.","personality_traits":["patient","resilient","wary","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Mastery","description":"Keeps mills running in any wind and rations grain through shortages.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_ilan_quill","name":"Ilan Quill","role":"antagonist","description":"A gaunt Silverspine Academy cartographer in his sixties with ink-stained fingers and a pale cloak embroidered with chart lines. Once a respected Warden ally, he secretly sells skybridge maps to whoever pays, and now to the common enemy.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To secure funds and recognition for the Academy's failing archives and his own legacy.","goal":"Trade the shifting bridge charts to the enemy in exchange for protection of Silverspine.","flaw":"Vanity makes him believe his knowledge entitles him to decide the archipelago's fate.","internal_conflict":"He loves the Academy's mission of knowledge but betrays the Wardens he swore to serve.","external_conflict":"Mara's investigations threaten to expose him, and the alliance depends on keeping the maps secret.","arc":"Ilan starts as a trusted scholar quietly selling charts. When Mara discovers a forged map and confronts him on the Silverspine bridges, he chooses to burn the stolen charts rather than be exposed, and surrenders to the Wardens' judgement. He ends disgraced yet finally owning his betrayal.","personality_traits":["vain","brilliant","secretive","bitter"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts the drifting bridge network with unmatched precision.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_corvin_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_asha","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Venn blames Corvin Asha's Cartel tolls for neglected bridges, so the two clash over the Toll War even as the alliance forces them to cooperate."},{"id":"rel_tessa_corvin_enemies","source_character_id":"chr_tessa_holloway","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_asha","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tessa Holloway resents Corvin Asha for the Grain Levy he enforces on the Hollow Circle's shipments."},{"id":"rel_mara_ilan_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_ilan_quill","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Ilan Quill taught Mara Venn to read bridge charts as a young Warden, so his betrayal cuts deeply and drives her to expose him."},{"id":"rel_mara_tessa_ally","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_tessa_holloway","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Venn and Tessa Holloway share a respect for honest labour and form an early bond against Cartel pressure."}]}
