n_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_corvin_hale","name":"Corvin Hale","description":"A 48-year-old merchant prince of the Drift Cartel, Corvin is lean and immaculate, with silver rings on every finger and a voice kept soft on purpose. He rose from a dockhand during the signing of the Cartel Charter's aftermath and now controls the busiest shipping lanes from Mistral Docks. He believes order is purchased, not given.","role":"antagonist","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's monopoly on the lanes so that no storm or war can ever return him to poverty.","goal":"Use the bridge collapse to justify permanent emergency tolls and sole control of all crossings.","flaw":"He measures everyone by price and cannot imagine loyalty that cannot be bought.","internal_conflict":"He privately suspects his own lieutenant's faction caused the collapse and fears learning it was done in his name.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist his tolls and levies, and Maren's investigation threatens to expose Cartel involvement.","arc":"Corvin starts as a calm profiteer who treats the disaster as opportunity. When Maren's logs show that sabotage used open flame smuggled aboard a Cartel barge, in violation of the no-fire rule, he must choose between burying evidence and a shipping blockade of his own docks. Facing the ruin of his lanes, he surrenders the guilty lieutenant and suspends tolls, ending diminished but forced to recognise obligations beyond price.","personality_traits":["calculating","soft-spoken","paranoid","charming"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane Brokerage","description":"Negotiates contracts and wind-debt settlements that bind entire islands.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_isolde_penn","name":"Isolde Penn","description":"A 27-year-old cartographer at Silverspine Academy, Isolde is small and ink-stained, with round spectacles and a satchel of folded charts. She grew up in the Academy's archives and has memorised the drift patterns of every skybridge. She is the first to notice that the collapsed bridge was deliberately cut.","role":"supporting","motivation":"To keep the truth of the network's shape on record so that knowledge cannot be rewritten by the powerful.","goal":"Publish a corrected map showing the exact crossing point and timing of the sabotage.","flaw":"She is a conflict-averse bystander who hides in data rather than confront anyone.","internal_conflict":"She longs to be useful in the field but fears her cowardice will get people killed.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents pressure the Academy to suppress her chart, and her Academy superiors fear losing Cartel funding.","arc":"Isolde begins as a nervous archivist who keeps her findings private. When a Cartel agent offers a sinecure to burn her chart, she refuses and rides with Maren to the wreck to take measurements in person. She ends as a public witness who presents the chart at the Academy, no longer hiding behind her archives.","personality_traits":["shy","precise","observant","quietly brave"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Charting","description":"Predicts skybridge drift and wind shifts from historical records.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_tobias_wren","name":"Tobias Wren","description":"A 52-year-old miller of the Hollow, Tobias is broad-shouldered and flour-dusted, with a booming laugh gone quiet since the levy. He leads a Hollow Circle council that has fed half the archipelago through the Great Calm's lessons of self-reliance. His grain barges were stranded when the bridge fell.","role":"supporting","motivation":"To keep his people fed and free of Cartel debt.","goal":"Break the Grain Levy by securing a route for Hollow grain that bypasses Cartel lanes.","flaw":"He is distrustful of outsiders and holds grudges for decades.","internal_conflict":"He wants to protect his community's independence but knows isolation will starve it if the bridges stay down.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy bleeds his harvests, and stranded barges are accruing wind-debt he cannot repay.","arc":"Tobias begins by refusing to cooperate with Wardens or Cartel alike. When his stranded barges' wind-debt comes due, he accepts Maren's offer to haul cloudstone in exchange for debt forgiveness. Working beside islanders he once resented, he ends as an advocate for the unified isles and a bridge-builder in his own right.","personality_traits":["gruff","generous","proud","resilient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Logistics","description":"Coordinates large grain milling and transport efforts across isles.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"},{"id":"chr_sable_quill","name":"Sable Quill","description":"A 29-year-old Cartel lieutenant at Mistral Docks, Sable is sharp-featured with a shaved head and a rust-coloured coat. She came up through the docks' smuggling underworld and answers to Corvin in public but resents his caution. She quietly arranged the sabotage to force emergency powers on the Cartel.","role":"antagonist","motivation":"To seize control of the Cartel from a leader she thinks too timid.","goal":"Frame the Wardens for the collapse and push Corvin into declaring war on them.","flaw":"Her ambition makes her reckless and blind to consequences she did not plan.","internal_conflict":"She convinced herself the deaths were necessary but is haunted by a child's cap she found at the wreck.","external_conflict":"Maren's investigation closes in on her, and Corvin begins to doubt her loyalty.","arc":"Sable starts as a confident schemer certain the sabotage will elevate her. When Maren and Isolde's chart traces the spark to her barge, she tries to burn the evidence with open flame at the docks, in violation of the no-fire rule, and nearly severs another bridge. Horrified, she confesses to Corvin and gives herself up, ending as a disgraced but finally honest figure.","personality_traits":["ambitious","sharp-tongued","restless","guilt-ridden"],"abilities":[{"name":"Dock Intrigue","description":"Moves contraband and information through the docks unseen.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_corvin_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Voss accuses Corvin Hale of profiting from the collapse, while Corvin uses Cartel influence to block her access to the wreck and discredit the Wardens."},{"id":"rel_maren_isolde_allies","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_penn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Voss relies on Isolde Penn's charts to trace the sabotage, and in turn pushes Isolde out of the archives into fieldwork."},{"id":"rel_corvin_sable_patron","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","target_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Corvin Hale elevated Sable Quill from the docks, but she resents his caution and secretly works against his authority, creating a rift that fuels the plot."},{"id":"rel_tobias_corvin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tobias Wren resists the Grain Levy Corvin Hale imposed on Hollow harvests, and neither will yield without a crisis forcing them together."},{"id":"rel_maren_tobias_allies","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Voss trades wind-debt forgiveness to Tobias Wren for his barges and labour, forming an uneasy partnership to rebuild the crossing."},{"id":"rel_sable_maren_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Sable Quill plans to frame Maren Voss and the Wardens for the collapse, and later tries to destroy the evidence Maren is following."}]}
