rself up, ending as a disgraced but finally honest figure.","personality_traits":["ambitious","sharp-tongued","restless","guilt-ridden"],"abilities":[{"name":"Dock Intrigue","description":"Moves contraband and information through the docks unseen.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_corvin_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Voss accuses Corvin Hale of profiting from the collapse, while Corvin uses Cartel influence to block her access to the wreck and discredit the Wardens."},{"id":"rel_maren_isolde_allies","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_penn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Voss relies on Isolde Penn's charts to trace the sabotage, and in turn pushes Isolde out of the archives into fieldwork."},{"id":"rel_corvin_sable_patron","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","target_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Corvin Hale elevated Sable Quill from the docks, but she resents his caution and secretly works against his authority, creating a rift that fuels the plot."},{"id":"rel_tobias_corvin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tobias Wren resists the Grain Levy Corvin Hale imposed on Hollow harvests, and neither will yield without a crisis forcing them together."},{"id":"rel_maren_tobias_allies","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Voss trades wind-debt forgiveness to Tobias Wren for his barges and labour, forming an uneasy partnership to rebuild the crossing."},{"id":"rel_sable_maren_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","desc