[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_maren_voss","name":"Maren Voss","description":"A weathered Bridge Warden engineer in her forties, stationed at Emberroost. She has braided cloudstone cable since girlhood and her hands are scarred by cable burns. Raised on the forge-island, she wears a soot-stained leather apron and keeps a notched measuring rod that belonged to her father. She is quiet and exacting, and she distrusts anything that cannot be measured.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges standing so the isles she grew up with are not cut off from one another.","goal":"Find and repair the failing wards on the main skybridge anchors before the next season's drift.","flaw":"Rigid pride in her own craft makes her refuse help and dismiss warnings she did not discover herself.","internal_conflict":"She suspects the old wards were built on arcane power the kingdom outlawed, and she must weigh that against her lifelong loyalty to the law.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls starve her crews of funds and labour while the wards decay.","arc":"Maren begins as a proud engineer who hides the wards' failure to protect her guild's reputation. After a cable snap at Emberroost proves the wards are failing and the Cartel's toll war blocks repair funding, she chooses to publicly share her findings and accept help from rivals. She ends as a humbler leader who values collaboration over solitary pride.","personality_traits":["exacting","stubborn","loyal","taciturn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and splicing load-bearing cloudstone cable.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Structural diagnosis","description":"Can judge a bridge's stress and wear by sound and touch.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_hale","name":"Corvin Hale","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel merchant prince based at Mistral Docks. Broad-shouldered and impeccably dressed in dark wool with brass buttons, he controls a fleet of cargo skiffs. He rose from a dockhand to a charter holder and never forgets it.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure permanent wealth and safety for himself after a childhood of dockside poverty.","goal":"Raise skybridge tolls and the grain levy to lock in Cartel control of all inter-isle trade.","flaw":"Greed that blinds him to the risks of starving the bridges of maintenance.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears the bridges are failing and that his wealth rests on a collapsing network.","external_conflict":"The Bridge Wardens and the Hollow Circle both resist his tolls and levy.","arc":"Corvin starts as a confident profiteer who denies the wards are failing. When Maren presents proof and a bridge near the Docks nearly collapses with his cargo aboard, he faces the cost of his tolls. He ends by diverting toll revenue to repairs, at the price of his absolute control.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","paranoid"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade negotiation","description":"Persuades and pressures rivals into favourable contracts.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_penn","name":"Isolde Penn","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy, barely twenty, with ink-stained fingers and a habit of sketching in the margins of everything. Orphaned by a bridge accident, she was taken in by the Academy's archivists.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To understand why the bridge that killed her parents failed, so no one else suffers the same loss.","goal":"Chart the pattern of ward failures across the skybridge network and identify the next point of collapse.","flaw":"Impulsive, she acts on half-finished data and overstates her conclusions.","internal_conflict":"She wants vengeance for her parents but is afraid of what the truth about the wards might reveal.","external_conflict":"The Academy's elders discourage her research because it questions the kingdom's founding law.","arc":"Isolde starts as an impulsive researcher who publishes unverified maps. When one of her premature warnings causes a panic at Mistral Docks, she learns to double-check her work with Maren's field measurements. She ends as a careful scholar whose verified map saves a bridge crossing.","personality_traits":["curious","impulsive","earnest"],"abilities":[{"name":"Network charting","description":"Maps shifting skybridge connections and predicts drift patterns.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tobiah_marsh","name":"Tobiah Marsh","description":"An elder miller of the Hollow Circle, stout and grey-bearded, whose windmills grind grain for half the archipelago. He remembers the Great Calm as a child and carries its lessons in every decision.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect the Hollow's farmers from the Cartel's grain levy and keep the archipelago fed.","goal":"Rally the Hollow Circle to withhold grain shipments until the levy is lifted.","flaw":"Distrust of outsiders makes him refuse compromise even when it would help his people.","internal_conflict":"He fears that withholding grain will starve the very isles he swore to feed.","external_conflict":"Corvin Hale's levy threatens to bankrupt the Hollow's farmers.","arc":"Tobiah begins as an inflexible elder who rejects any dealings with the Cartel. When a poor harvest and a stalled bridge strand his grain, he accepts an alliance with Maren's Wardens. He ends as a pragmatic negotiator who trades grain for bridge repairs.","personality_traits":["stubborn","protective","wise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Weather reading","description":"Predicts wind shifts and storms from the feel of the air.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_corvin_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Voss blames Corvin Hale's rising tolls for starving the Wardens of repair funds, and Corvin sees her warnings as a threat to his trade."},{"id":"rel_isolde_maren_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_penn","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Isolde Penn looks to Maren Voss for field knowledge to ground her charts, while Maren is reluctantly drawn to Isolde's data."},{"id":"rel_tobiah_corvin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_tobiah_marsh","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tobiah Marsh opposes Corvin Hale's grain levy, which threatens the Hollow's farmers."},{"id":"rel_maren_tobiah_ally","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobiah_marsh","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Voss and Tobiah Marsh become allies against the Cartel, trading bridge repairs for grain."}]}
