[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_venn","name":"Mara Venn","description":"A thirty-four-year-old Bridge Warden engineer raised on Emberroost, Mara has braided cloudstone cable since childhood and carries rope-scarred hands and a cropped streak of grey in her dark hair. After a cable she certified frayed and stranded a crew for a night, she began sleeping badly. She is the first to notice that a strange crystal, a dreamstone, is pulling the islanders into the same dream.","role":"protagonist","motivation":"To prove her skill and make the skybridges safe, so that no crossing ever again costs lives through her oversight.","goal":"Trace the shared dream to the dreamstone and sever its hold on the islands before the dreams weaken the skybridges' upkeep.","flaw":"Perfectionism that makes her distrust anyone's work but her own.","internal_conflict":"She is drawn to the comfort of the shared dream, where the stranded crew never suffered, yet fears that surrendering to it means abandoning her duty.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls and the Toll War strip the Wardens of resources just as she needs them to contain the dreamstone.","arc":"Mara begins by trusting only her own hands and hiding her nightly dreams. During the Toll War, when Cartel pressure leaves Emberroost short-handed, she must hand a forge-pit crew the final cable braiding while she follows the dream to its source. They succeed, and she ends by leading a shared team and accepting imperfect help.","personality_traits":["meticulous","guarded","dry-humoured","tireless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Expert at weaving and inspecting cloudstone cable by touch.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Dream Sensitivity","description":"Feels the pulse of the dreamstone as a faint hum in her sleep.","category":"supernatural"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_oren_calloway","name":"Oren Calloway","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel factor in his fifties at Mistral Docks, Oren wears a salt-stained coat of ink-blue velvet and a ring for every shipping lane he controls. He has bought and sold whole cargoes of dreams and debts alike. When the dreamstone surfaces, he sees only a monopoly.","role":"antagonist","motivation":"To secure a lasting place among the Cartel's princes by owning the most valuable commodity in the archipelago.","goal":"Seize the dreamstone and sell access to the shared dream, and so raise the wind-debt owed to the Cartel.","flaw":"Greed that blinds him to consequences he cannot price.","internal_conflict":"He privately dreads dying forgotten and unmourned, and the dreams show him the faces of those he has ruined.","external_conflict":"The Toll War makes the Wardens his obstacle, and the Grain Levy stirs the Hollow Circle against him.","arc":"Oren starts as a confident profiteer who dismisses the dreams as a novelty. When the Grain Levy backlash starves Mistral Docks and the dream shows him a farmer he ruined, he tries to hoard the dreamstone anyway. He ends exposed and stripped of his lane, forced to repay a wind-debt in honest labour.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Persuades crowds and councils to bend to his terms.","category":"social"},{"name":"Lane Mastery","description":"Reads wind currents and shipping lanes better than any pilot.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_tamsin_reed","name":"Tamsin Reed","description":"A weathered miller of twenty-nine from The Hollow, Tamsin has flour-dusted forearms and a habit of humming to the windmills. She loses her whole harvest ledger to the Cartel's Grain Levy and starts dreaming of fields that never burn. The Hollow Circle sends her to learn what is spreading through their sleep.","role":"supporting","motivation":"To keep her neighbours fed and free from Cartel debt.","goal":"Carry the Hollow Circle's case against the Grain Levy to the Wardens and gain their protection.","flaw":"Stubborn pride that makes her refuse help even when she is drowning.","internal_conflict":"She wants to escape into the peaceful dream of full granaries but feels guilty for deserting the people who rely on her.","external_conflict":"Oren's Cartel levy threatens to take the Hollow's grain and crush the Hollow Circle.","arc":"Tamsin begins isolated, grinding grain alone and refusing aid. After a Cartel enforcer seizes a grain shipment under the Grain Levy, she crosses the skybridge to Emberroost and accepts Mara's help. She ends as the Hollow Circle's voice in the archipelago, willing to rely on allies.","personality_traits":["stubborn","warm","practical","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind Reading","description":"Predicts gusts and calms from the turning of the windmill sails.","category":"physical"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"},{"id":"chr_isolde_quill","name":"Isolde Quill","description":"A young cartographer of twenty-three at Silverspine Academy, Isolde has ink-stained cuffs and wide, sleepless eyes. Her maps of the drifting skybridges begin to show routes that appear only in the shared dream, and she cannot decide whether they are errors or revelations.","role":"supporting","motivation":"To be recognised as a cartographer whose discoveries matter beyond the Academy's walls.","goal":"Chart the dream-routes and locate the dreamstone's origin before the Cartel does.","flaw":"Reckless curiosity that makes her ignore warnings and rules.","internal_conflict":"She wants scholarly proof but is tempted to fabricate certainty so her findings will be believed.","external_conflict":"Oren's agents want her maps, and the Academy's elders fear she will bring scandal on the Wardens' network.","arc":"Isolde begins as an eager mapper who inflates her findings. When Oren offers to buy her dream-route charts, she nearly sells them, then burns a false chart in a shielded forge-pit and gives Mara honest, uncertain data instead. She ends as a trusted, honest scholar.","personality_traits":["curious","impulsive","brilliant","anxious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts shifting skybridge networks with uncanny accuracy.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_oren_rival","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_oren_calloway","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Venn opposes Oren Calloway because his tolls strain the Wardens and he wants to monopolise the dreamstone she is trying to contain."},{"id":"rel_oren_mara_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_oren_calloway","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Oren Calloway sees Mara Venn as the engineer who stands between the Cartel and the profits of the dreamstone, and works to cut off her supplies."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tamsin Reed turns to Mara Venn for Warden protection against the Cartel's grain levy, an alliance built on shared hostility toward Oren."},{"id":"rel_isolde_mara_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_quill","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Mara Venn mentors Isolde Quill, steadying her reckless curiosity and teaching her to value honest data over impressive claims."},{"id":"rel_oren_isolde_rival","source_character_id":"chr_oren_calloway","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_quill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Oren Calloway tempts Isolde Quill with payment for her dream-route maps, pressing her toward the dishonesty she is struggling to resist."}]}
</Output>
