{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_wren_halloway","name":"Wren Halloway","description":"A twenty-six-year-old Bridge Warden apprentice with wind-chapped cheeks, soot-darkened fingers, and a coil of braided cloudstone cord always looped at her belt. Raised in the forge-island of Emberroost by a cable-braider father who died when a bridge snapped, she joined the Wardens to make sure no other family suffers the same loss.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To honor her father's memory by making every skybridge crossing safe for ordinary families.","goal":"Expose and repair the faulty cable stock that is being sold to the Wardens and causing bridge failures.","flaw":"Reckless self-reliance; she refuses help and takes on dangerous repairs alone.","internal_conflict":"She fears that her father's death was due to his own negligence, and that proving it would taint his legacy.","external_conflict":"The Toll War pits the Wardens against the Drift Cartel, which pressures her superiors to cut corners on bridge maintenance.","arc":"Wren begins as a lone, driven apprentice who trusts only her own hands. During the Toll War she attempts a solo emergency repair of a failing bridge and nearly falls, saved only by Corvin's crew, forcing her to see that safety is a shared labour. She ends as a team leader who shares credit and accepts the truth about her father.","personality_traits":["determined","stubborn","observant","dry-humoured"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and splicing cloudstone cable under tension.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Stress Reading","description":"Can sense weakness in a cable by sound and vibration.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_vale","name":"Corvin Vale","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel merchant prince in his forties, dressed in storm-blue coats lined with brass buttons and rings stamped with shipping-lane marks. He rose from a dockhand at Mistral Docks to command dozens of freight skiffs.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure his family's fortune and never again be a penniless dockhand under the wind-debt.","goal":"Raise skybridge tolls and impose a grain levy to cement Cartel control of all inter-isle trade.","flaw":"Pride that cannot tolerate being seen as dependent on anyone.","internal_conflict":"He privately knows the rising tolls starve the isles he grew up among and is ashamed of what he has become.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle both resist his tolls and levy, threatening his Cartel standing.","arc":"Corvin starts as a confident profiteer who justifies every toll as business. When the Grain Levy sparks a shortage at The Hollow and his own dock crews go hungry, he is forced to confront the cost of his policy. He ends by cutting the tolls and pledging Cartel ships to move grain at cost, losing wealth but regaining self-respect.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","proud","secretly guilt-ridden"],"abilities":[{"name":"Shrewd Negotiator","description":"Reads motives and bends deals in his favour.","category":"social"},{"name":"Wind-lane Navigation","description":"Knows every shipping lane and gust pattern between isles.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ilsa_thorne","name":"Ilsa Thorne","description":"A quiet Hollow Circle miller in her fifties, broad-shouldered and flour-dusted, with silver-streaked braids and a limp from an old windmill accident. She has run the largest mill on The Hollow since the Great Calm, when she rationed grain for her neighbours.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep the archipelago fed and her community independent.","goal":"Organise the farmers to resist the Cartel's grain levy without starting open violence.","flaw":"Distrust of outsiders that makes her reject useful allies.","internal_conflict":"She wants peace but suspects that only confrontation will protect her people.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy drains the Circle's stores and the Cartel threatens to cut off their shipping.","arc":"Ilsa begins as an insular miller who refuses to speak to Wardens or merchants. After the levy leaves The Hollow short of seed grain, she accepts Wren's offer of Warden escorts for a grain convoy. She ends as an open coalition builder who links the Circle to the Wardens.","personality_traits":["patient","wary","resourceful","gruff"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Reckoning","description":"Can estimate harvest yields and stores precisely.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_odalys_finch","name":"Odalys Finch","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy, thin and ink-stained, with spectacles tied on by a ribbon. She charts the drift of the skybridge network and has a fierce curiosity about the First Weaving.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To understand why the bridges drift and to prove that scholarship can protect lives.","goal":"Complete a drift map that predicts which skybridges will fail.","flaw":"Naive faith in data that makes her ignore human motives.","internal_conflict":"She wants academic recognition but fears her maps will be used by the Cartel to raise tolls.","external_conflict":"The Cartel offers to fund her work in return for exclusive access to her maps, while the Wardens need them freely.","arc":"Odalys starts as a sheltered scholar who treats her maps as neutral. When Corvin's agent tries to buy her predictions to price bridge tolls, she sees how her data could cause harm. She ends by giving the maps to Wren's Wardens and publishing them openly.","personality_traits":["curious","earnest","anxious","brilliant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Prediction","description":"Forecasts skybridge drift from wind-current charts.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_wren_corvin_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_wren_halloway","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_vale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Wren Halloway blames Corvin Vale's Cartel tolls and cheap cable stock for the bridge failures, and Corvin sees Wren as an obstacle to his Toll War strategy."},{"id":"rel_corvin_ilsa_levy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_vale","target_character_id":"chr_ilsa_thorne","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Vale imposes the Grain Levy on Ilsa Thorne's mill, while Ilsa organises the Hollow Circle to resist him."},{"id":"rel_wren_ilsa_alliance","source_character_id":"chr_wren_halloway","target_character_id":"chr_ilsa_thorne","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Wren Halloway offers Warden escorts to Ilsa Thorne's grain convoys, forming an uneasy alliance against the Cartel."},{"id":"rel_odalys_wren_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_finch","target_character_id":"chr_wren_halloway","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Odalys Finch supplies Wren Halloway with drift predictions, and Wren teaches Odalys how bridges behave in the field."},{"id":"rel_corvin_odalys_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_vale","target_character_id":"chr_odalys_finch","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Corvin Vale pressures Odalys Finch to sell her drift maps to the Cartel, which she resists."}]}
