_id":"loc_mistral_docks","motivation":"To never again be poor and powerless as he was as a dockhand.","goal":"Raise tolls and impose the grain levy to cement Cartel control of every shipping lane.","flaw":"Greed that makes him see people as debts to be collected.","internal_conflict":"He privately knows the Cartel's tolls are hastening the bridge decay that threatens his own trade.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist his tolls and levy, and the Cartel's own wind-debt ledgers expose him.","arc":"Starts as a confident profiteer dismissing bridge warnings. When a Warden report by Isolde proves a toll-starved bridge could cut his main shipping lane, he must choose between short-term profit and survival of his trade. He ends by cutting tolls for repair, a calculated but real concession that exposes his fear of ruin.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","paranoid"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Mastery","description":"Tracks wind-debts and shipping contracts across the archipelago.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Negotiates favourable terms from nearly anyone.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","name":"Tamsin Reeve","description":"A broad-shouldered young miller from The Hollow with flour-dusted forearms, sun-freckled skin, and a quick laugh. She grew up during stories of the Great Calm and learned self-reliance from her grandmother.","role":"supporting","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","motivation":"To keep her community fed and free of Cartel debt.","goal":"Get the Grain Levy overturned by forming an alliance with the Wardens.","flaw":"Naive trust in people who flatter her community.","internal_conflict":"She wants to stay in the quiet Hollow but feels the pull to fight for it in the wider world.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy threatens to bankrupt her family mill.","arc":"Begins as a homebody who avoids politics. When the Cartel levy seizes