{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_isolde_vane","name":"Isolde Vane","description":"A weathered Bridge Warden engineer in her thirties, with soot-stained hands, a braid threaded with copper wire, and a coat patched with cloudstone fibre. She grew up on Emberroost braiding cables beside her father, who fell when a spark severed a span.","role":"protagonist","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","motivation":"To honour her father's death by making every skybridge safe from fire and neglect.","goal":"Secure a toll-free maintenance charter so the Wardens can reinforce the failing bridges before the next storm season.","flaw":"Stubborn perfectionism that makes her refuse help and delay decisions.","internal_conflict":"She fears that her obsession with safety is really a way to avoid grieving her father.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls starve the Wardens of funds during the Toll War, while she needs to repair bridges now.","arc":"Starts as a lone, rigid engineer who trusts only her own work. When a toll-blocked bridge near Emberroost nearly collapses because she delayed a patch waiting for perfect materials, she accepts Hollow Circle labour and imperfect repairs from Tamsin Reeve. She ends as a leader who delegates and grieves openly.","personality_traits":["meticulous","stubborn","loyal","dry-humoured"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and splicing cloudstone cables under tension.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Spark Discipline","description":"Instinctively spots fire hazards and controls forge-pits.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_halloway","name":"Corvin Halloway","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel merchant prince in his fifties, tall and immaculately dressed in sailcloth silks, with rings stamped by the Cartel Charter. He rose from a dockhand at Mistral Docks.","role":"antagonist","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","motivation":"To never again be poor and powerless as he was as a dockhand.","goal":"Raise tolls and impose the grain levy to cement Cartel control of every shipping lane.","flaw":"Greed that makes him see people as debts to be collected.","internal_conflict":"He privately knows the Cartel's tolls are hastening the bridge decay that threatens his own trade.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist his tolls and levy, and the Cartel's own wind-debt ledgers expose him.","arc":"Starts as a confident profiteer dismissing bridge warnings. When a Warden report by Isolde proves a toll-starved bridge could cut his main shipping lane, he must choose between short-term profit and survival of his trade. He ends by cutting tolls for repair, a calculated but real concession that exposes his fear of ruin.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","paranoid"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Mastery","description":"Tracks wind-debts and shipping contracts across the archipelago.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Negotiates favourable terms from nearly anyone.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","name":"Tamsin Reeve","description":"A broad-shouldered young miller from The Hollow with flour-dusted forearms, sun-freckled skin, and a quick laugh. She grew up during stories of the Great Calm and learned self-reliance from her grandmother.","role":"supporting","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","motivation":"To keep her community fed and free of Cartel debt.","goal":"Get the Grain Levy overturned by forming an alliance with the Wardens.","flaw":"Naive trust in people who flatter her community.","internal_conflict":"She wants to stay in the quiet Hollow but feels the pull to fight for it in the wider world.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy threatens to bankrupt her family mill.","arc":"Begins as a homebody who avoids politics. When the Cartel levy seizes her family's grain stores, she travels to Emberroost and offers labour in exchange for Warden support, a pivotal choice that tests her trust. She ends as a confident envoy who verifies promises before trusting.","personality_traits":["warm","practical","optimistic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Craft","description":"Builds and repairs windmills and reads wind patterns.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Community Organiser","description":"Rallies farmers and millers to act together.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_oswin_pell","name":"Oswin Pell","description":"An elderly cartographer at Silverspine Academy, thin and stooped, with ink-stained fingers and thick lenses. He has charted the shifting skybridge network for four decades and keeps a secret map of failing spans.","role":"supporting","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","motivation":"To leave behind a complete, accurate map of the network.","goal":"Publish his map of failing bridges so the Wardens can prioritise repairs.","flaw":"Cowardice about conflict, hiding data to avoid controversy.","internal_conflict":"He values scholarly neutrality but knows silence endangers lives.","external_conflict":"The Cartel pressures the Academy to suppress data that could disrupt trade.","arc":"Starts as a timid scholar hoarding his findings. When Isolde shows him a bridge that fails exactly where his map predicted, he chooses to publish despite Cartel pressure. He ends as a public voice for bridge safety.","personality_traits":["meticulous","timid","wise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Predicts drift patterns and bridge stress points.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_halloway","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Vane blames Corvin Halloway's tolls for starving the Wardens of repair funds, while Corvin sees her as an obstacle to Cartel control."},{"id":"rel_corvin_tamsin_levy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_halloway","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Corvin Halloway imposes the grain levy that threatens Tamsin Reeve's family mill, and she resists him."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_isolde_allies","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tamsin Reeve offers Hollow Circle labour to Isolde Vane in exchange for Warden backing against the Cartel."},{"id":"rel_oswin_isolde_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_oswin_pell","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Oswin Pell shares his maps of failing bridges with Isolde Vane and guides her repair priorities, while she pushes him to publish."}]}
