{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_isolde_vance","name":"Isolde Vance","description":"A lean, wind-weathered woman in her thirties with rope-scarred palms and a braid of silver-streaked black hair. Born on Emberroost to a family of cable-braiders, she rose to Senior Warden after her father fell when a severed skybridge dropped him into the clouds. She wears a soot-stained Warden's coat stitched with cloudstone thread.","role":"protagonist","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","motivation":"To honour her father's death by making every skybridge safe from sabotage and greed.","goal":"Unite the three royal houses long enough to defend the skybridge network from the thing stirring beneath the ice.","flaw":"Stubborn pride that makes her refuse help from anyone she suspects of profiting from the bridges.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect everyone but secretly believes only she can be trusted to do it right.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls strangle the Wardens' funding while the royal houses compete for the throne.","arc":"Starts as a rigid, solitary guardian who distrusts all merchants. During the Toll War, a Cartel ship crew risks its vessel to save a collapsing bridge she could not hold alone. She accepts shared command of the bridge defence and ends as a coalition builder who delegates authority.","personality_traits":["disciplined","stubborn","loyal","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Can braid and repair skybridge cable at speed under high wind.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Wind Reading","description":"Senses shifts in wind currents that foretell bridge stress.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_halewright","name":"Corvin Halewright","description":"A broad-shouldered, silver-tongued merchant prince in his fifties, with rings on every finger and a gambler's smile. Heir to a Cartel dynasty at Mistral Docks, he signed the tolls into law and lives surrounded by ledgers and bodyguards.","role":"antagonist","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","motivation":"To secure his family's dynasty by owning the shipping lanes and a seat of influence beside the next throne.","goal":"Back a royal claimant who will make the Cartel Charter permanent and tolls untouchable.","flaw":"Greed that blinds him to threats that cannot be priced.","internal_conflict":"He fears his late father's contempt and cannot tell whether he builds wealth for his family or to prove himself.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle both resist his tolls and grain levy, threatening his political backing.","arc":"Begins as a confident profiteer dismissing rumours from the ice as superstition. When a toll-funded fleet is lost to the awakened enemy and the Grain Levy sparks a famine riot, he must choose between profit and survival. He opens Cartel ships to evacuations at a ruinous cost, ending humbled and no longer ruled by his ledger.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","persuasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Negotiates and bribes his way through almost any dispute.","category":"social"},{"name":"Lane Mastery","description":"Knows every shipping lane and wind current in the archipelago.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_orchard","name":"Tamsin Orchard","description":"A sturdy, sun-browned miller in her twenties with flour-dusted hair and calloused hands. She runs the largest windmill on The Hollow and speaks for the Hollow Circle in disputes. She is quiet by habit but unshakeable when pressed.","role":"supporting","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","motivation":"To keep her neighbours fed and free of debt after surviving the lean years of the Great Calm stories her grandmother told.","goal":"Defeat the Cartel's Grain Levy without starving the isles that depend on The Hollow.","flaw":"Avoidance of confrontation leads her to delay decisions until they are forced.","internal_conflict":"She longs for a peaceful life but knows peace requires her to stand publicly against the powerful.","external_conflict":"The Cartel levy threatens to bankrupt the Hollow Circle's farmers and leave isles hungry.","arc":"Starts as a reluctant spokesperson who hides behind committee votes. When Cartel enforcers seize a grain shipment, she walks alone onto Mistral Docks to demand its release before the crowd. She ends as the Hollow Circle's confident leader, willing to speak first.","personality_traits":["patient","practical","warm","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Sense","description":"Judges harvests and storage needs of whole isles by feel and smell.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_leander_ashgrove","name":"Leander Ashgrove","description":"A thin, ink-stained cartographer in his forties with spectacles and a perpetually crumpled scholar's robe. He teaches at Silverspine Academy and has charted the skybridges for two decades. Rumoured to hold maps no one else has seen.","role":"supporting","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","motivation":"To complete the definitive chart of the shifting skybridge network before his failing eyesight ends his work.","goal":"Prove through his charts that the ice beneath the archipelago is changing and convince the royal houses to act.","flaw":"Cowardice about confronting authority, leading him to hedge or hide his findings.","internal_conflict":"He values truth above all but fears the consequences of sharing it with powerful people.","external_conflict":"Royal advisers and Cartel agents dismiss or suppress his charts as alarmist.","arc":"Starts by burying his findings in footnotes to avoid trouble. After Isolde Vance's bridge crew is nearly lost because he withheld a warning, he publishes the full ice charts openly to the Academy. He ends as a vocal witness willing to be unpopular.","personality_traits":["meticulous","timid","curious","absent-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Predicts drift patterns and bridge shifts from charts and long observation.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_brannock_dray","name":"Brannock Dray","description":"A scarred, imposing former Cartel enforcer in his forties with a shaved head and a heavy limp. Born at Mistral Docks, he now drifts between jobs and carries a Warden's cast-off coat he cannot explain keeping.","role":"supporting","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","motivation":"To escape the debt of violence he has collected for Corvin Halewright and prove he is more than a hired fist.","goal":"Earn enough in honest labour to repay his wind-debt and leave the Cartel's service.","flaw":"Resentment he nurses over past wrongs, which turns quickly into violence.","internal_conflict":"He wants redemption but believes he is too far gone to deserve it.","external_conflict":"Corvin Halewright holds his contract and a wind-debt that binds him to enforcement work.","arc":"Starts as a bitter enforcer sent to intimidate Tamsin Orchard's millers. Seeing her stand unarmed against his crew, he refuses the order and defends the shipment. He ends as an ally of the Hollow Circle, repaying his debt in labour.","personality_traits":["gruff","loyal","brooding","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Dockside Brawling","description":"Fights effectively in close quarters on narrow platforms and decks.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_toll_war","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vance","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_halewright","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Vance blames Corvin Halewright's tolls for starving the Wardens of funds and for her father's unmaintained bridge. Corvin sees her as an obstacle to Cartel profit, fueling the Toll War."},{"id":"rel_corvin_brannock_employer","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_halewright","target_character_id":"chr_brannock_dray","relationship_type":"employer","description":"Corvin Halewright holds Brannock Dray's wind-debt and uses him as an enforcer, binding him to work he despises."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_corvin_levy","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orchard","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_halewright","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tamsin Orchard resists Corvin Halewright's Grain Levy on behalf of the Hollow Circle, while Corvin pressures her to submit."},{"id":"rel_leander_isolde_ally","source_character_id":"chr_leander_ashgrove","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vance","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Leander Ashgrove supplies Isolde Vance with his skybridge charts, though his hesitancy to speak up nearly costs her crew their lives."},{"id":"rel_brannock_tamsin_redemption","source_character_id":"chr_brannock_dray","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orchard","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Brannock Dray, sent to intimidate Tamsin Orchard, is moved by her courage and turns to defend her and the Hollow Circle."},{"id":"rel_isolde_tamsin_ally","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vance","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orchard","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Vance and Tamsin Orchard join forces against Cartel pressure, with Tamsin teaching Isolde to share leadership."}]}
