{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kestrel_vane","name":"Kestrel Vane","description":"A lean, sharp-eyed rigger-turned-smuggler in her thirties who sells her knowledge of skybridge routing to anyone who pays. Raised in the rope-sheds of Mistral Docks, she wears a patched windcoat and carries a tally-slate of every wind-debt she has dodged. Her hands are scarred from cloudstone cable. She is the one who lifts a sealed corporate seed-core, a living cartel ledger-mind, from the Drift Cartel vaults.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"Wants to erase the crushing wind-debt that has bound her family to Cartel labour for three generations.","goal":"Sell the stolen seed-core to a buyer who can clear her family's debt ledger for good.","flaw":"Treats every person as a transaction and trusts nobody, so she pushes away potential allies.","internal_conflict":"She despises the Cartel yet has built her whole identity on being useful to its machinery.","external_conflict":"The Cartel brands her the most wanted person in the archipelago and hunts her across every skybridge.","arc":"Starts as a cynical mercenary who sees the seed-core as a payday. When the Cartel burns a bridge-crossing to trap her and Wardens are caught in it, she must choose between selling the core and handing it to the Bridge Wardens to expose the toll scheme. She gives it up, losing her payday, and ends as a wary but committed ally who accepts shared risk.","personality_traits":["cynical","resourceful","guarded","darkly witty"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Routing","description":"Knows hidden crossings and wind patterns that evade Cartel toll checkpoints.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Seed-Core Intrusion","description":"Breaks into sealed ledger-mind vaults and bypasses their locks.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_orsolya_thane","name":"Orsolya Thane","description":"A silver-haired Cartel merchant princess in her fifties, polished and soft-spoken, who runs the Mistral Docks shipping lanes from a glass-walled counting-house. She wears layered navy brocade and rarely raises her voice. She signed her first toll ledger at nineteen and has never lost a negotiation.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"Wants to make Cartel control of inter-isle trade permanent and unchallengeable.","goal":"Recover the stolen seed-core before its contents reveal how tolls are inflated, and crush Kestrel as an example.","flaw":"Cannot tolerate being outmaneuvered, so she escalates minor losses into disproportionate retaliation.","internal_conflict":"She privately fears the toll system she built is hollow and will collapse without constant force.","external_conflict":"The Toll War with the Bridge Wardens and the Grain Levy resistance threaten her monopoly as the theft exposes her.","arc":"Begins as a composed strategist certain of her control. When the Hollow Circle refuses the grain levy and the Wardens publish the seed-core data, her overreaction to the leak triggers a cartel revolt among her own merchants. She ends stripped of her seat, forced to confront that fear-driven control was what destroyed her.","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","vindictive","controlled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Toll Leverage","description":"Sets wind-debt rates and shipping lane access to coerce rivals and officials.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_halloway","name":"Bram Halloway","description":"A broad-shouldered Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, forties, with soot-darkened forearms and a limp from a snapped cable years ago. He is methodical and dry-humored, and keeps a worn braiding tool that belonged to his mentor.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"Wants to keep the skybridges safe after watching a cable failure kill his crew.","goal":"Prove that Cartel-inflated tolls are starving maintenance budgets and endangering the bridges.","flaw":"Rigid rule-follower who refuses help from anyone who has broken the law.","internal_conflict":"He knows the Wardens' lawful channels are failing but fears that bending rules makes him no better than the Cartel.","external_conflict":"The Toll War leaves his crews underfunded while the Cartel pressures the Wardens to cooperate.","arc":"Starts as a by-the-book engineer who would arrest Kestrel on sight. After the Cartel sabotages a crossing and Kestrel's route knowledge saves his crew, he chooses to shield her and use the seed-core data in a public hearing. He ends willing to bend procedure for the bridges' sake.","personality_traits":["methodical","stubborn","dry-humored","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Braids and repairs cloudstone skybridge cables under stress.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_marrow","name":"Isolde Marrow","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy, twenty-six, with ink-stained fingers and a habit of talking to herself while charting. She is brilliant and sheltered, recently tasked with mapping skybridge shifts for Wardens and Cartel alike.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"Wants to prove that careful knowledge can protect the archipelago from corrupt power.","goal":"Decode the seed-core's records and verify that tolls were manipulated.","flaw":"Naive about danger and overshares findings with people she assumes are honest.","internal_conflict":"She idolizes the academy's neutrality yet feels cowardly hiding behind it.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents pressure the Academy to hand over her work and silence her.","arc":"Starts as a sheltered scholar who believes neutrality is safe. After Cartel agents seize her charts and she narrowly escapes via Kestrel's route, she publicly testifies about the data's authenticity. She ends as a visible, courageous witness who accepts the cost of taking sides.","personality_traits":["curious","earnest","anxious","meticulous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Network Charting","description":"Maps and predicts skybridge network shifts and data patterns.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_reed","name":"Tamsin Reed","description":"A weathered Hollow Circle miller in her sixties, with flour-dusted gray braids and a calm, unhurried voice. She leads the quiet resistance to the grain levy from her windmill on The Hollow and remembers the Great Calm firsthand.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"Wants to keep her community fed and independent as it was after the Great Calm.","goal":"Defeat the grain levy and secure a fair shipping rate for Hollow grain.","flaw":"Stubborn pride makes her refuse compromise even when it would save lives.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect her people but fears dragging them into open conflict.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy and shipment blockades threaten to starve The Hollow into submission.","arc":"Starts as a patient holdout hoping to wait the Cartel out. When blockades cause a shortage and Kestrel smuggles grain through, she accepts alliance with outsiders and joins the Wardens' hearing. She ends as an open leader of resistance, trading pride for solidarity.","personality_traits":["patient","proud","resilient","wise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Community Organizing","description":"Rallies farmers and millers to act together.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_orsolya_hunts_kestrel","source_character_id":"chr_orsolya_thane","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Orsolya Thane hunts Kestrel Vane for stealing the seed-core, using Cartel bounties and toll lockdowns to corner her."},{"id":"rel_kestrel_bram","source_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","target_character_id":"chr_bram_halloway","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Kestrel Vane and Bram Halloway begin as wary opponents but become allies after her routes save his crew."},{"id":"rel_isolde_kestrel","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Marrow decodes the seed-core Kestrel Vane stole, and Kestrel protects her from Cartel agents."},{"id":"rel_bram_orsolya","source_character_id":"chr_bram_halloway","target_character_id":"chr_orsolya_thane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Bram Halloway opposes Orsolya Thane over inflated tolls that starve Warden maintenance budgets."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_orsolya","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_orsolya_thane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tamsin Reed resists Orsolya Thane's grain levy and blockades on The Hollow."},{"id":"rel_kestrel_tamsin","source_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Kestrel Vane smuggles grain past Cartel blockades to Tamsin Reed, earning her reluctant trust."}]}
