{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kestrel_vane","name":"Kestrel Vane","description":"A lean, sharp-eyed rigger-turned-smuggler in her thirties who sells her knowledge of skybridge routing to anyone who pays. Raised in the rope-sheds of Mistral Docks, she wears a patched windcoat and carries a tally-slate of every wind-debt she has dodged. Her hands are scarred from cloudstone cable. She is the one who lifts a sealed corporate seed-core, a living cartel ledger-mind, from the Drift Cartel vaults.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"Wants to erase the crushing wind-debt that has bound her family to Cartel labour for three generations.","goal":"Sell the stolen seed-core to a buyer who can clear her family's debt ledger for good.","flaw":"Treats every person as a transaction and trusts nobody, so she pushes away potential allies.","internal_conflict":"She despises the Cartel yet has built her whole identity on being useful to its machinery.","external_conflict":"The Cartel brands her the most wanted person in the archipelago and hunts her across every skybridge.","arc":"Starts as a cynical mercenary who sees the seed-core as a payday. When the Cartel burns a bridge-crossing to trap her and Wardens are caught in it, she must choose between selling the core and handing it to the Bridge Wardens to expose the toll scheme. She gives it up, losing her payday, and ends as a wary but committed ally who accepts shared risk.","personality_traits":["cynical","resourceful","guarded","darkly witty"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Routing","description":"Knows hidden crossings and wind patterns that evade Cartel toll checkpoints.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Seed-Core Intrusion","description":"Breaks into sealed ledger-mind vaults and bypasses their locks.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_orsolya_thane","name":"Orsolya Thane","description":"A silver-haired Cartel merchant princess in her fifties, polished and soft-spoken, who runs the Mistral Docks shipping lanes from a glass-walled counting-house. She wears layered navy brocade and rarely raises her voice. She signed her first toll ledger at nineteen and has never lost a negotiation.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"Wants to make Cartel control of inter-isle trade permanent and unchallengeable.","goal":"Recover the stolen seed-core before its contents reveal how tolls are inflated, and crush Kestrel as an example.","flaw":"Cannot tolerate being outmaneuvered, so she escalates minor losses into disproportionate retaliation.","internal_conflict":"She privately fears the toll system she built is hollow and will collapse without constant force.","external_conflict":"The Toll War with the Bridge Wardens and the Grain Levy resistance threaten her monopoly as the theft exposes her.","arc":"Begins as a composed strategist certain of her control. When the Hollow Circle refuses the grain levy and the Wardens publish the seed-core data, her overreaction to the leak triggers a cartel revolt among her own merchants. She ends stripped of her seat, forced to confront that fear-driven control was what destroyed her.","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","vindictive","controlled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Toll Leverage","description":"Sets wind-debt rates and shipping lane access to coerce rivals and officials.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_halloway","name":"Bram Halloway","description":"A broad-shouldered Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, forties, with soot-darkened forearms and a limp from a snapped cable years ago. He is methodical and dry-humored, and keeps a worn braiding tool that belonged to his mentor.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"Wants to keep the skybridges safe after watching a cable failure kill his crew.","goal":"Prove that Cartel