er fifties, polished and soft-spoken, who runs the Mistral Docks shipping lanes from a glass-walled counting-house. She wears layered navy brocade and rarely raises her voice. She signed her first toll ledger at nineteen and has never lost a negotiation.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"Wants to make Cartel control of inter-isle trade permanent and unchallengeable.","goal":"Recover the stolen seed-core before its contents reveal how tolls are inflated, and crush Kestrel as an example.","flaw":"Cannot tolerate being outmaneuvered, so she escalates minor losses into disproportionate retaliation.","internal_conflict":"She privately fears the toll system she built is hollow and will collapse without constant force.","external_conflict":"The Toll War with the Bridge Wardens and the Grain Levy resistance threaten her monopoly as the theft exposes her.","arc":"Begins as a composed strategist certain of her control. When the Hollow Circle refuses the grain levy and the Wardens publish the seed-core data, her overreaction to the leak triggers a cartel revolt among her own merchants. She ends stripped of her seat, forced to confront that fear-driven control was what destroyed her.","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","vindictive","controlled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Toll Leverage","description":"Sets wind-debt rates and shipping lane access to coerce rivals and officials.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_halloway","name":"Bram Halloway","description":"A broad-shouldered Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, forties, with soot-darkened forearms and a limp from a snapped cable years ago. He is methodical and dry-humored, and keeps a worn braiding tool that belonged to his mentor.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"Wants to keep the skybridges safe after watching a cable failure kill his crew.","goal":"Prove that Cartel