{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_voss","name":"Mara Voss","role":"protagonist","description":"A 38-year-old night-shift radio host who left Mistral Docks after a failed career in port dispatch. She now broadcasts a late-night call-in show from a lone cabin, which is both her studio and her home. She is lean and sleepless, with ink-stained fingers, a wool coat she never takes off, and a voice that has gone gravelly from years of whispering into microphones.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","motivation":"To prove her isolation was a choice and not an exile, by keeping her broadcast alive and her mind intact.","goal":"Identify the source of the transmissions and stop the future broadcast she hears before it comes true.","flaw":"She trusts her own control over every situation and will not accept help or admit she is afraid.","internal_conflict":"She fears the voice from the future is proof she is losing her mind, yet she also fears it is real and that her death is already written.","external_conflict":"The transmissions give her precise warnings that she can only avoid by breaking the shielded-flame rule she lives under, and the Cartel levy cuts off the supplies she needs to keep the cabin running.","arc":"Mara starts out isolated and certain she can handle anything alone. In the pivotal moment, the future voice tells her to light the cabin lamp, breaking the open-flame ban that Hollow Circle neighbours enforce. Neighbour Ilsa Brandt stops her and shows her the signal is steering her toward harm. Mara admits her fear aloud on air and accepts Ilsa's help. She ends the story still frightened but willing to rely on others, which breaks her habit of solitary control.","personality_traits":["stubborn","observant","dry-humoured","insomniac"],"abilities":[{"name":"Signal Tuning","description":"Can isolate faint transmissions from heavy static by ear and by adjusting the equipment.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Calming Voice","description":"Her steady on-air delivery can settle panicked listeners.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ilsa_brandt","name":"Ilsa Brandt","role":"supporting","description":"A 55-year-old Hollow Circle miller who lives in the nearest farmstead and delivers grain and supplies to the cabin. She is broad-shouldered and weathered, with flour-dusted sleeves and a habit of counting everything twice. She remembers the Great Calm from childhood.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep her community fed and safe, as it was during the Great Calm.","goal":"Keep Mara alive and the cabin supplied while the Grain Levy squeezes the Hollow's shipments.","flaw":"She hoards worry and quietly over-manages other people's lives.","internal_conflict":"She wants to respect Mara's privacy but feels guilty about every sign of trouble she ignores.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy leaves her short on stock, forcing her to ration what she delivers to the cabin.","arc":"Ilsa begins as a distant, controlling helper who leaves goods on the doorstep and keeps her fears to herself. When the grain levy tightens and Mara reaches for a flame, Ilsa forces her way inside and stops her. Afterwards she stays and listens to the broadcasts with Mara instead of managing from afar. She ends as an equal partner who trusts Mara to share the burden.","personality_traits":["blunt","protective","practical"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Reckoning","description":"Can estimate stores and shortfalls at a glance.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_corin_thale","name":"Corin Thale","role":"antagonist","description":"A 45-year-old Drift Cartel levy agent with a courteous manner and a pressed grey coat. He once worked the Mistral Docks ledgers and now collects grain levies on remote isles. He listens to Mara's broadcasts and recognises a profitable opportunity in the strange signal.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure a promotion by delivering Cartel control over every remote voice and supply line.","goal":"Seize Mara's transmitter and the future signal and sell it to the Cartel's merchant princes.","flaw":"He is greedy and treats people as line items, ignoring warning signs that a deal is too good.","internal_conflict":"He privately doubts that the Cartel will reward him and fears he has spent his career serving masters who would discard him.","external_conflict":"The Hollow Circle resists his levy, and the Cartel council demands results before the season's wind-debt comes due.","arc":"Corin starts as a confident collector who sees the signal as an asset. He comes to the cabin to take the transmitter and hears a transmission that predicts his own ruin if he keeps the equipment. Rattled, he tries to bargain the Cartel's levy for the signal and is refused by Ilsa and Mara. He leaves empty-handed, the first time his greed has cost him something, and chooses to stop pursuing the signal.","personality_traits":["polite","calculating","ambitious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Leverage","description":"Uses debts and wind-debt records to pressure people into compliance.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_ilsa_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_ilsa_brandt","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilsa Brandt is Mara Voss's closest ally and supplier, and her protective hovering strains Mara's insistence on independence."},{"id":"rel_corin_mara_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corin_thale","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corin Thale targets Mara Voss's transmitter and uses supply pressure to force her to give up the signal."},{"id":"rel_corin_ilsa_rival","source_character_id":"chr_corin_thale","target_character_id":"chr_ilsa_brandt","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Corin Thale presses Ilsa Brandt to pay the Cartel grain levy, and she resists him to protect the Hollow Circle."}]}
