ane","description":"A young junior cartographer at Silverspine Academy, Tobias is lanky and ink-stained, with spectacles repaired by cloudstone wire. He charted the map that was stolen and feels responsible for it.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that careful cartography serves the whole archipelago and not just the powerful.","goal":"Help recover the map and correct the false copies the thieves are circulating.","flaw":"He is naive and trusts anyone who shows interest in his work.","internal_conflict":"He longs for adventure beyond the library but is terrified of leaving the safety of the Academy.","external_conflict":"The Wardens suspect him of leaking the map, and the Cartel wants him to chart routes for them.","arc":"Tobias starts as a timid scholar who trusts too easily. When Brannoch Dusk flatters him into revealing a chart-cipher and he is then blamed for the theft, he learns to verify his sources. He ends as a confident field cartographer who travels the skybridges with Kaelen.","personality_traits":["earnest","curious","anxious","precise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"He can chart and recall the shifting skybridge network with exceptional accuracy.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_brannoch_dusk","name":"Brannoch Dusk","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel merchant prince at Mistral Docks, broad-shouldered and impeccably dressed in indigo silk with rings of cloudstone. He commissioned the theft of the map to monopolise every skybridge route.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure total control of inter-isle trade and make the Cartel's tolls unchallengeable.","goal":"Use the stolen map to seize the key skybridge crossings and force the Wardens and Hollow Circle to submit.","flaw":"His arrogance leads him to underestimate people he considers beneath him.","interna