{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kaelen_rooke","name":"Kaelen Rooke","description":"A weathered former skyship raider in her late thirties, Kaelen Rooke once commanded the Gale Magpie and plundered Cartel cargo across the isles until a botched raid cost her crew their lives. She now works as a dock-hand and quiet fixer at Mistral Docks. She has wind-burned skin, a braided rope of grey-streaked black hair, and a scar across her palm from a cut skybridge cable.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","motivation":"To atone for the crew she lost by recovering the stolen map that could restore the livelihoods of those she harmed.","goal":"Recover the stolen skybridge map before it is used to seize control of the archipelago's crossings.","flaw":"She distrusts any authority and assumes everyone will eventually betray her, so she hides crucial information from allies.","internal_conflict":"She wants redemption but secretly believes she is incapable of being anything other than a raider.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel is hunting her for old crimes while she crosses skybridges that accrue wind-debt she cannot easily repay.","arc":"Kaelen begins as a solitary, guilt-ridden dock-hand who withholds information from everyone. At Silverspine Academy, when Tobias is arrested because she hid the map's true significance, she confesses everything to the Bridge Wardens and shares the burden of the search. She ends as a trusted leader who accepts help and chooses a lawful path over raiding.","personality_traits":["wry","guarded","resourceful","fiercely loyal in secret"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windreading","description":"She can sense shifts in wind currents and predict storms and drift patterns.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Dockside Cant","description":"She speaks the coded slang of smugglers and dockhands, gaining quiet access to underworld informants.","category":"social"}],"faction_id":null},{"id":"chr_tobias_vane","name":"Tobias Vane","description":"A young junior cartographer at Silverspine Academy, Tobias is lanky and ink-stained, with spectacles repaired by cloudstone wire. He charted the map that was stolen and feels responsible for it.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that careful cartography serves the whole archipelago and not just the powerful.","goal":"Help recover the map and correct the false copies the thieves are circulating.","flaw":"He is naive and trusts anyone who shows interest in his work.","internal_conflict":"He longs for adventure beyond the library but is terrified of leaving the safety of the Academy.","external_conflict":"The Wardens suspect him of leaking the map, and the Cartel wants him to chart routes for them.","arc":"Tobias starts as a timid scholar who trusts too easily. When Brannoch Dusk flatters him into revealing a chart-cipher and he is then blamed for the theft, he learns to verify his sources. He ends as a confident field cartographer who travels the skybridges with Kaelen.","personality_traits":["earnest","curious","anxious","precise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"He can chart and recall the shifting skybridge network with exceptional accuracy.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_brannoch_dusk","name":"Brannoch Dusk","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel merchant prince at Mistral Docks, broad-shouldered and impeccably dressed in indigo silk with rings of cloudstone. He commissioned the theft of the map to monopolise every skybridge route.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure total control of inter-isle trade and make the Cartel's tolls unchallengeable.","goal":"Use the stolen map to seize the key skybridge crossings and force the Wardens and Hollow Circle to submit.","flaw":"His arrogance leads him to underestimate people he considers beneath him.","internal_conflict":"He fears the Cartel will discard him if his scheme fails, and this clashes with his belief that he rules by merit.","external_conflict":"The Toll War with the Bridge Wardens and the Grain Levy dispute with the Hollow Circle threaten his hold on the trade.","arc":"Brannoch begins as a confident, untouchable power broker. When Kaelen and Mara expose his scheme during the Grain Levy dispute, the Cartel council turns against him. He ends stripped of his seat, forced to face the fear of being disposable that drove him.","personality_traits":["charming","ruthless","vain","calculating"],"abilities":[{"name":"Market Manipulation","description":"He bends shipping lanes and debts to ruin rivals and bind allies.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_mara_ellory","name":"Mara Ellory","description":"A stern Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost in her fifties, with soot-darkened forearms and a limp from a bridge collapse. She is devoted to the safety of the skybridges.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe and prevent another collapse like the one that crippled her.","goal":"Stop the Cartel from using the map to weaken key crossings, and bring the thieves to Warden justice.","flaw":"She is rigid and refuses to bend rules even when they cause harm.","internal_conflict":"She believes in lawful order but suspects the Wardens' neutrality has let the Cartel grow strong.","external_conflict":"The Toll War puts her at odds with the Cartel, and her superiors forbid her from working with a known pirate.","arc":"Mara begins as an inflexible enforcer who sees Kaelen as a criminal. When Kaelen confesses at Silverspine and offers the map's location, Mara bends the Wardens' rules to ally with her. She ends as a pragmatic leader willing to challenge her own order's inertia.","personality_traits":["disciplined","blunt","protective","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Engineering","