over from The Hollow who joined Marra's caravan to see beyond the windmills. He has sandy hair always dusted with flour, ink-stained fingers from sketching bridges, and a battered satchel of borrowed maps.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To see the whole archipelago and prove a farm boy can be more than a miller's son.","goal":"Chart a safe route for the caravan over the shifting bridges and earn a place at Silverspine Academy.","flaw":"Naive eagerness; he trusts anyone who is kind to him.","internal_conflict":"He feels guilty for leaving his family during the Grain Levy while craving adventure.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents try to use him to learn which isles hold unlevied grain.","arc":"Begins as a trusting, homesick boy chasing adventure. When Cartel agent Corvin Dray befriends him and asks about hidden grain stores, Tobin realises he nearly betrayed his home and chooses to refuse and warn Marra. He ends as a wary but confident navigator who values loyalty to his people over flattery.","personality_traits":["curious","earnest","gullible","hardworking"],"abilities":[{"name":"Route Sketching","description":"Quickly maps skybridge networks from memory and observation.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_dray","name":"Corvin Dray","description":"A polished Drift Cartel factor in his forties, Corvin wears a tailored sky-blue coat with brass buttons and a ring from every major dock. He is soft-spoken, smiling, and always carrying a ledger bound in grey leather.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure a seat among the Cartel's merchant princes by enforcing their tolls and levies.","goal":"Seize control of Marra's caravan and the Hollow's grain shipments for the Cartel.","flaw":"Ambition that makes him treat people as ledger entries.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears he is a hired hand who will never be accepted by the princes he serves.","external_conflict":"The Wardens block his toll collection and Marra's independence undermines his quota.","arc":"Starts as a charming enforcer certain loyalty will earn him status. When Marra's open ledger exposes the Cartel's inflated tolls and his superiors disown him to save face, Corvin must choose between covering up and testifying. He ends diminished but honest, giving evidence that shifts the Grain Levy, or stays bitter if he refuses, a choice that tests his fear of being expendable.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","insecure","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Contract Law","description":"Uses wind-debt terms to bind merchants to unfavourable deals.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ilsa_forge","name":"Ilsa Forge","description":"A muscular Bridge Warden engineer in her thirties from Emberroost, with soot-darkened forearms, a cropped haircut, and a belt of cloudstone splicing tools. She is blunt, tireless, and takes pride in every cable she braids.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe so nobody falls because of greed.","goal":"Repair the severed skybridge and keep it open despite Cartel tolls and sabotage.","flaw":"Rigid distrust of merchants; she assumes all traders serve the Cartel.","internal_conflict":"She resents that her duty to the bridges forces her to cooperate with the very merchants she distrusts.","external_conflict":"The Toll War starves the Wardens of funds and materials while the Cartel pressures them.","arc":"Begins suspicious of every merchant, including Marra. When Marra's caravan delivers cloudstone cable at its own cost to finish a bridge repair, Ilsa sees a merchant act for the common good. She ends as an ally who vouches for honest traders and brokers a fair crossing agreement.","personality_traits":["blunt","diligent","proud","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description"